{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115874-wolves-of-hell-brainstorming-forsaken-inferno-game-possibly-idigam-chronicles","id":115874,"title":"Wolves of Hell - Brainstorming Forsaken + Inferno game ( Possibly Idigam Chronicles )","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-19T08:19:27-07:00","id":115874,"title":"Wolves of Hell - Brainstorming Forsaken + Inferno game ( Possibly Idigam Chronicles )","content":"So I'm mosltly Mage ST and was having rought time with <b>Forsaken</b> before. I played it under other ST for couple of sessions in 2006, but come to conclusion that it's not game for me. But lately I was convinced to give it a next try by whole <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click\"> Werewolf as a Roleplay Game</a> topic. There were idea to run game with <b>Maeljin</b> and their &quot;devil worshiping&quot; Bale Hounds based on story of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thiess_of_Kaltenbrun\" target=\"_blank\">Thiess of Kaltenbrun</a>. I was wanting to run <b>Inferno</b> game before, I would love to inrocpoate here, with a bit of Possesed added to the mix. So here is my chronicle idea, and would want you to tell me what more I need to read or preper.<br /> <br /> Players are inhabitnatce of american/european small town. Once in couple of days they are all attacked by &quot;big dogs&quot; and have near death expirance. Quicly they found out they are &quot;wolf-mans&quot;, chaning in to rabid beast at various phases of moon. At fris they can't control it, slowly they come to realisation they can under light of specific moons. They think of themsvles as cursed and looks for the beast that runed them in first place. They got a trail of Bale Hounds that &quot;sacrifice they souls for Lords of Infero&quot; and changed in to werewolves. Characters now need to become &quot;proper&quot; Uratha and destroy the cult/pack that runs the town to save themselves. Finally, they must go to &quot;the Hell and back&quot; by Wounds to end the threat of Lords of Inferno. That's basic idea.<br /> <br /> I know it's won't be typical <b>Werewolf</b> game, but to me werewolves are best serve as &quot;spawn of Satan', that players need to remake in to &quot;more human&quot; monsters. I was thinking about using Cursed from <b>Forsaken's Chronicle Guide</b>, but they are too much one sided. I want players chracters to grow from thinking they are simple beasts that kills towns people under the moon, to Uratha hunters of proper setting, &quot;unmaking their curse&quot;. <br /> <br /> Looking over Wolf-Blooded of <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> they probably will be perfect for first part of chronicle, with slowly making those Wolf-Blooded in to proper Uratha by the half of story. I'm interested could they be used in this way?<br /> <br /> And we have towns pack/cult of Seven Demon Lords, each leaded by one Bale Hound. What info I will need for this? Are there good <b>Frosaken</b>/<b>Inferno</b> crossover info, bsiede the later itself?<br /> <br /> Finally, how could Shadow of tha kind of setting looked like? Were is more info on Wounds? Could it be connected with Hell of <b>Inferno</b>?<br /> <br /> Side question \u2013 could <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> help me with this game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T12:39:32-07:00","id":116040,"title":"","content":"Well it looks like a creative idea and I think it could work.<br /> <br /> One idea to make sure that the character goes in the right general direction is to throw in some kind of mentor figure to help them.<br /> <br /> But anyway the big thing for me is that I don't really see the need for demons from the Inferno supplement here. Also isn't the Lords of the Inferno and the Maeljin rather different things? And between the Bale Hounds and the Maeljin I don't see the need for the demons. One idea could be to skip the Bale Hounds and simply roll with some Uratha who'se made some kind of deal with the demons.<br /> <br /> In regards to crossover info I can't come up with a single source. There are good books detailing the Maeljin and the Bale Hounds, but in regards to Inferno? No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T13:22:15-07:00","id":116062,"title":"","content":"Oh boy I get to geek out slightly about obscure pseudo-canon in nWoD.<br /> <br /> Assuming you have the Inferno book there's a direct crossover with Werewolf. Demons can corrupt just about anything and when they manage to corrupt a spirit the hybrid entity is called an Immundi (vampire lore buffs might recognize this term) and they're often associated with Wounds and the legions of the Maeljin. The Maeljin themselves are counted as Rank 8 Demons (Dukes of Hell) and are likely extremely powerful Immundi.<br /> <br /> More information on Wounds, the Maeljin, and Bale Hounds can be found in Lore of the Forsaken and Blasphemies with the Former having a ton of info on Wounds and Maeljin and the latter having some pretty useful stuff on the forces of the Maeljin and the Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T23:29:24-07:00","id":116357,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <b>Red 9</b>, for reading recomendations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115874-wolves-of-hell-brainstorming-forsaken-inferno-game-possibly-idigam-chronicles?p=116040#post116040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea to make sure that the character goes in the right general direction is to throw in some kind of mentor figure to help them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking maybe of ex-pack/cult member. Maybe even it's him who makes PCs in werewolves, knowing that he himself can't fight with cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115874-wolves-of-hell-brainstorming-forsaken-inferno-game-possibly-idigam-chronicles?p=116040#post116040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But anyway the big thing for me is that I don't really see the need for demons from the Inferno supplement here. Also isn't the Lords of the Inferno and the Maeljin rather different things? And between the Bale Hounds and the Maeljin I don't see the need for the demons. One idea could be to skip the Bale Hounds and simply roll with some Uratha who'se made some kind of deal with the demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to add human element to the story - mayor and other local council memebers <b>are</b> huamn, nad still they help Bale Hounds because of their dedication to Dukes of Hell. Think of cult mixed werewolf movie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T04:16:56-07:00","id":116439,"title":"","content":"Probably I will still idea from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115031-uratha-cultures\">Uratha Cultures</a> topic and run as Scandinavian game, probably in Sweden... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T03:17:28-07:00","id":122256,"title":"","content":"Two question come to my mind forum users could help me - I need cool name for small, sinister town for setting in English. I will then transalte it to the Swedish and make it even more sinister... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, what Auspice/Tribe combination would be good for mentor figure? To make a bit twist, I think about She-Wolf that was expelled from ruling Bale Hounds Pack. She reconnects with her Firstborn Tribal spirit and want to pass on &quot;werewolves blessing&quot; to players. As I read corebook Bale Hounds technically are still members of they starting Tribes, so great Seven ( now 8 ) would be from each diffrent Tribe and divided town on regions they guards.<br /> <br /> And here is She-Wolf... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/PVzljDmoPVs\" data-code=\"PVzljDmoPVs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PVzljDmoPVs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Even Gifts are shown!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T04:20:06-07:00","id":125115,"title":"","content":"Very well video and I'm happy that those wolves/that wolf gav the hunters wha thy had coming for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T04:52:07-07:00","id":125125,"title":"","content":"Great to hear that! Still would love to read about cool idea for town's name and mentor Auscpice/Tribe combination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:38:10-07:00","id":174568,"title":"","content":"I'm returning to my original idea, as chronicle now have about one month long. The title of the game changed to &quot;Hounds of Hell&quot; as better sounding by players ( they call ). Characters are 5 young Uratha that in time of last two weeks were mostly Wolf-Blooded - I needed to ruch things a bit with character transformation as players were a bit impatient. PCs mentor is ex-Hound of Lust Irraka She-Wolf that wnats to use new Forsaken pack for ravange on her once Bale Hunds comrades. She helped them get a bear Totem, and Winter Wolf seeing how resourceful are PCs, he made them from Wolf-Blooded to Uratha. Now they are taking care of they new territory on the boarders of valley inside Scandinavian Mountains.<br /> <br /> And here we come to me next idea for chronicle - PCs will look for the klaives and fetishes left by ancient Uratha hero, Norse-like legendary figure. There will be local story of him as brave viking commander and &quot;helped by gods and spirits&quot;. He would be blessed by All-Father-Thunder and his court that now PCs will need to find and convince to work with them. Here is a bit about two spirits from there:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136808#post136808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think All-Father-Thunder would have to be pushed up to a Rank 7. He\u2019s going to be the spirit created by all those feelings and thoughts and actions based on an all-powerful, father-like figure from the sky. That means he\u2019s going to have aspects of Odin, Zeus, Ra, YHVH, etc, etc, etc. This figure is all over the place in Europe, which makes it insanely powerful. Major Influences would be things like lightning and thunder, clouds and wind, wisdom and justice, authority and law. This is also the spirit of all those high kings and divinely allowed overlords of the universe. I think it would appear as either a lion or a bull, and it\u2019s kind of hard to tell sometimes because he\u2019s surrounded with rumbling thunder and dark clouds, especially when angry\u2026.which is often the reason he appears. When he\u2019s coming in a gentler aspect, there would be a light shining thru the clouds as if from above. He can be the aspect of authority as a punisher and as a protector, but he\u2019s rarely subtle or light-trodding.<br /> <br /> The Crash Before The Storm is one of his harbingers. A little storm crow made up of that buzzing in the air before a storm. The wind that brings the smell of ozone to let you know what\u2019s coming. Probably no more than a Greater Gaffling (Rank 2), might make it to Lesser Jaggling while attached to a pack. Influences would be wind and sounds (low thunder in the background), a little bit of premonition based on fore-shadowing and warning signs, speed and flight (since it always has to stay ahead of the storm)\u2026.no more than 2 dots in each. Numina \u2013 Blast, Chorus, Reaching (for little blasts of air), Wilds Sense (so it knows where All-Father-Thunder is at all times). Higher Finesse and Resistance than Power. This little guy isn\u2019t about power, it\u2019s about warning people about the in-coming power!</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem/idea is simple - how to call this Uratha-viking hero character from early Dark Ages? PCs will need to find his burial place to get klaives and rest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}